<title>UK: CRICKET-ENGLISH COUNTY CHAMPIONSHIP SCORES.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-ENGLISH COUNTY CHAMPIONSHIP SCORES.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Close of play scores on the</p>
<p>third day of four-day English County Championship cricket</p>
<p>matches on Friday:</p>
<p>At Derby: Sussex 200-9 declared. Derbyshire 233-9 (V.Clarke</p>
<p>65 not out, C.Adams 53; V.Drakes 4-55, R.Kirtley 4-98).</p>
<p>At Bath: Leicestershire 442-6 declared (J.Whitaker 133 not</p>
<p>out, I.Sutcliffe 112, V.Wells 70, D.Maddy 58). Somerset</p>
<p>72-2.</p>
<p>At Trent Bridge: Yorkshire 364 all out (D.Byas 128,</p>
<p>D.Lehmann 62, M.Moxon 60; K.Evans 6-91). Nottinghamshire 148-7</p>
<p>(C.White 4-51).</p>
<p>At Darlington: Durham 251 all out and 183-8 (M.Speight 73</p>
<p>not out; M.Fleming 4-34). Kent 167 all out (M.Betts 7-29)</p>
<p>At Northampton: Hampshire 405-8 declared (M.Hayden 150,</p>
<p>R.Smith 74, D.James 56; P.Taylor 6-91). Northamptonshire 40-2.</p>
<p>At Liverpool: Glamorgan 173-1 (S.James 99 not out) v</p>
<p>Lancashire. No play because of rain.</p>
<p>At Bristol: Middlesex 237 all out and 78-6 (J.Lewis 4-34).</p>
<p>Gloucestershire 99 all out (R.Johnson 4-27). No play because of</p>
<p>rain.</p>
<p>At Worcester: Surrey 452-9 declared (J.Ratcliffe 135,</p>
<p>A.Brown 121; S.Lampitt 4-104). Worcestershire 81-1. No play</p>
<p>because of rain</p>
</text>
